        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ломтик",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ломтик (lómtik) — \"a slice\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Она положила на тарелку два ломтика сыра. Oná polozhíla na tarélku dva lómtika sýra. She put two slices of cheese on the plate."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Diminutive of ломоть \"a hunk, a slice\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ломтик (lómtik) is a diminutive of ломоть \"a hunk of bread\", built on the root of ломать \"to break\": a piece broken off. EtymDB lists no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
